\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  Butler: government has no higher priority than strengthening general practice, but no answer on raising Medicare rebate }{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum
\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  Andrew Wilkie gets the next crossbench question and it is to Mark Butler, the minister for health. (I missed the question, but it is on whether or not the government will fix the GP Medicare issues by raising the rebate)}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2  Butler: }{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 I thank the member for Clark for his question because he knows there\u8217 s never been harder, never more expensive to see a doctor than it is right now in Australia and is no mystery why, Mr Speaker. It is a direct result of nine long years of cuts and neglect to Medicare, because they began when the leader of the opposition was the minister for health.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 We remember, Mr Speaker, that we managed to block his original radical plan to impose a GP tax on every single Australian going to the doctor, but he was determined \u8230  to hack into Medicare funding and so instead he imposed a freeze on Medicare rebates for lasted six long years. A pay freeze on the nation\u8217 s GPs while their costs were going up... this has created unprecedented pressure on billing rates.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 The former government was allergic to telling the truth about bulk billing, but \u8230  the truth is that one in three Australians now are paying a gap [fee] to see their doctor. \u8230  The number is increasing and the gap has never been higher than it is right now.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 For the first time in Medicare\u8217 s history, the average gap fee for you to see a doctor right now is higher than the Medicare rebate itself \u8230  that is why strengthening Medicare was the centrepiece of the Labor government[\u8217 s election commitment].}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 We brought together doctors, nurses, patient groups and others in the task force that I chair, leading up to Chris Schmidt, to advise the government on the best way to invest those funds. Mr Speaker, they will be different views within the task force but as we saw last week, when you bring people together in a respectful...}
