\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 As I have said before, we can\u8217 t fool ourselves with the concept of \u8216 striking a balance\u8217  when the reality has been a profound imbalance against nature.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0
\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Wilson said the future of Australia\u8217 s environment would require governments to become more \u8220 uncompromising\u8221  about the protection of Australia\u8217 s unique wildlife and ecosystems.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 This would mean not subscribing to the view that \u8220 any and every form of environmental impact can be approved provided [there] is a sufficient economic benefit\u8221 .}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard
