\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 It has to be said that under Anthony Albanese\u8217 s social media posts on suicide prevention today are legions of comments of people speaking about the financial stress the low jobseeker rate has put them under and how that is impacting their mental health.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 And it is not as easy as saying \u8220 just get a job\u8221 . Not everyone is able to take up work because of chronic health difficulties or disabilities \u8211  they are not able to commit to all of their shifts because of their medical needs. Others are unable to find meaningful work because they are spending all their time and energy trying to survive on a payment which consigns them to poverty. Others are working, but not receiving enough stable pay to be able to leave the social security system and others still are trapped by the gig economy.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 We know what lifting people out of poverty can do \u8211  we saw it during the pandemic. There are no plans to raise the jobseeker rate at the next budget in October.}{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb240\sa0
